## Why This Is Asked
Tests counting paths with variable step lengths using DP, a common interview pattern in operations and logistics contexts.

## Key Concepts
- 1D DP for path counting
- Handling variable jump lengths
- Modulo arithmetic for large counts

## Code Example
```javascript
function countWays(jumps){
  const n = jumps.length;
  const MOD = 1000000007;
  const dp = new Array(n).fill(0);
  dp[0] = 1;
  for(let i = 0; i < n; i++){
    const maxJump = Math.min(jumps[i], n - 1 - i);
    for(let s = 1; s <= maxJump; s++){
      dp[i + s] = (dp[i + s] + dp[i]) % MOD;
    }
  }
  return dp[n - 1] || 0;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you optimize to O(n) time if maxJump can be large but jumps form a sliding window of contributions?
- How would you adjust for different termination criteria or multiple destinations?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to combine subarray maxima with partition DP, requiring both maximization and reconstruction of multiple intervals. It exercises careful indexing and boundary handling.

## Key Concepts
- Non-overlapping subarrays with a cap k
- Precomputation of maxSub for O(1) subarray maxima
- 2D DP with reconstruction pointers
- Time/space tradeoffs and edge cases (k=0, equal values)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxValueWithKSubarrays(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const maxSub = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let l = 0; l < n; l++) {
    let m = -Infinity;
    for (let r = l; r < n; r++) {
      m = Math.max(m, A[r]);
      maxSub[l][r] = m;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(0));
  const take = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      let best = dp[i-1][t];
      let bestJ = -1;
      for (let j = 1; j <= i; j++) {
        const val = maxSub[j-1][i-1] + dp[j-1][t-1];
        if (val > best) { best = val; bestJ = j; }
      }
      dp[i][t] = best; take[i][t] = bestJ;
    }
  }
  const res = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
    const j = take[i][t];
    if (j === -1) break;
    res.push([j-1, i-1]);
    i = j - 1;
    t--;
  }
  res.reverse();
  return {value: dp[n][k], subarrays: res};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP over subsequences with a fixed length and pairwise costs, plus explicit reconstruction. It moves beyond contiguous partitions by requiring last-step linkage through prior picks.

## Key Concepts
- Subsequence DP with fixed length
- Min-over-predecessor recurrence
- Path reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time/space trade-offs and practical optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
function solve(A, m){
  const n=A.length;
  const dp=Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(m+1).fill(Infinity));
  const par=Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(m+1).fill(-1));
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) dp[i][1]=0;
  for(let t=2;t<=m;t++){
    for(let i=t-1;i<n;i++){
      for(let j=t-2;j<i;j++){
        const c=dp[j][t-1]+Math.abs(A[i]-A[j]);
        if(c<dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=c; par[i][t]=j; }
      }
    }
  }
  let best=Infinity,bestI=-1;
  for(let i=m-1;i<n;i++){ if(dp[i][m]<best){ best=dp[i][m]; bestI=i; } }
  const path=[];
  let cur=bestI, t=m;
  while(t>=1){
    path.push(cur);
    cur=par[cur][t];
    t--;
  }
  path.reverse();
  return {cost:best, indices:path};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to transform per-element cost into a standard max-sum DP for exactly k non-overlapping subarrays and to reconstruct endpoints. It emphasizes exact-k and non-overlap constraints common in analytics problems.

## Key Concepts
- Transform to B[i] = A[i] - c and reduce to max-sum of k non-overlapping subarrays
- DP states: local[i][t] for subarray ending at i; glob[i][t] for best so far with t subarrays
- Recurrences and reconstruction

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(B, k) {
  const n = B.length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const local = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const glob  = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  local[0][0] = 0; glob[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      local[i][t] = Math.max(local[i-1][t] + B[i-1], glob[i-1][t-1] + B[i-1]);
      glob[i][t] = Math.max(glob[i-1][t], local[i][t]);
    }
  }
  return {max: glob[n][k], endpoints: []};
}
```

